  "body": "## Problem\nA one-step negotiation ladder is valid in the backend, and the negotiation decision logic can correctly finish/reject an active one-step conversation without another offer. `RealActionPreflight`, however, treated every negotiating product with fewer than two configured steps as a hard failure whenever real next steps were armed.\n\nIn a multi-product bot this meant one valid one-step conversation could downgrade real next-step submission to dry-run for every other product, including products that still had valid next steps to send.\n\n## Changes\n- keep one-step negotiation ladders valid during `NEGOTIATION_CHECK` preflight\n- record a diagnostic note that such a conversation may finish without sending `NEXT_STEP`\n- preserve all existing ladder validation for empty, malformed, non-sequential, or non-positive steps\n- add regression coverage for:\n  - a single valid one-step MAIN negotiation\n  - an inactive one-step additional product coexisting with an active three-step product\n\n## Safety\nThis does not force a next step where none exists. `NegotiationDecisionService` remains responsible for deciding whether a conversation has a valid next step; when the ladder is exhausted it closes/surfaces the conversation without submitting another offer.\n\n## Tests\nFull repository CI is the merge gate. PR remains draft until all four jobs are green.",
